<[Wil] W.BADEN1> I recognized that F83 was very good,
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> and I accepted it as a standard.
<[Len] NMORGENSTERN> What they are doing at ANSI is the same: they are trying
<[Len] NMORGENSTERN> to standardize what is done, and what they think it should 
be
<[Len] NMORGENSTERN> sometimes switching from one to the other in one sentence.
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> The X is for extended or experimental, I never deciedd.
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> Say again, Len, u were scrampble.
<[Len] NMORGENSTERN> The people at ANSI were doing two things at the same time
<[Kevin] APPERT> even though they are charged with the task of codifing 
